    "pressure": {
      "file": "steam_distribution_header_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Dry steam at the right pressure",
      "description": "The header carries boiler-pressure steam. Branches leave from the top so they take dry steam, not the condensate that runs along the bottom. Drip legs of full header bore every ≈ 30–50 m (and at low points / before risers) collect condensate, which a trap removes; without them slugs of water cause water hammer and erosion. A PRV station drops the pressure for users that need lower pressure; latent heat per kg rises as pressure falls, and a downstream safety valve protects the low-pressure side.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
